# TinyStories Persona Patching (Pirate Style)

Stress tests, cosine similarity scoring, and a BERT style classifier for evaluating pirate-style persona patching on a TinyStories instruction-tuned chat model.

## Overview

This repository contains our final project for an LLM course. We trained a TinyStories instruction-tuned chat model, designed **three prompt stress-test sets**, and then **patched** the model using a targeted pirate-style dataset.

We compare the **baseline** and **patched** models using two evaluation methods:

- **Embedding cosine similarity** to pirate reference texts
- **BERT classifier** that estimates **P(pirate style | generated text)**

### Main Finding

Patching strongly increases pirate-style scores and also tends to make responses longer. However, scores remain very similar across all three prompt sets, suggesting that the patch mainly shifts the model’s **global style prior** rather than improving **prompt-conditioned instruction following**.

